Node ID=60 the queens favour
Text=<He is quiet for long enough that you can hear the fighting two chambers away.> Then you know more of this than I was going to tell you. The Queen keeps druids, Lionheart. She has kept them since before she had a throne, and what they bring her she does not ask twice about. My Order came to this shrine without her leave and we will be told off for it if we live. So we are both here doing England a service she has not asked for. Come on.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Then let us do it properly.
Go to node ID=10 accept
Icon=Quest Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=You are saying your own Queen protects them.
Go to node ID=61 she protects them

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=That changes nothing. Stand aside.
Go to node ID=
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=61 she protects them
Text=I am saying she has not moved against them, which in a Queen is the same thing. <He does not lower his voice, which tells you what he thinks of being overheard.> Whatever they are raising in there, she will call it hers when it is done, and the men who stopped it will have been brigands. Ask me again when we are out.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Then we had better not lose.
Go to node ID=10 accept
